entry.summary:
An x402 client pays whatever payTo the server puts in its 402 response. Budget caps answer "how much". Nothing in the default flow answers "to whom". So we gave our pay guard the Lazarus Group's wallet as the payTo of a real, healthy seller and asked whether to pay: curl "https://factline.dev/v1/pay/guard?url=https://api.onesource.io/&pay_to=0x098B716B8Aaf21512996dC57EB0615e2383E2f96&amount_usd=0.05&max_usd=1"
{ "decision": "deny", "reasons": ["payTo 0x098B716B8Aaf21512996dC57EB0615e2383E2f96 is on the OFAC sanctions list (LAZARUS GROUP)"], "seller": { "origin": "https://api.onesource.io", "known": true, "payers_30d": 321, "uptime_30d": 1, "median_ms": 1197 }, "ttl": 600 }
The seller itself is fine (321 paying wallets in 30 days, answered every nightly check). The wallet is not. …
